    "result_text": "A hold no longer takes a claim out of claimed. A held claim's amount, whether the claim itself is held or a person's hold covers its date, now counts in the person's claimed, the claimed-total, and the ROLLUP and TOTALS audit lines. Held claims still stay out of the due and overdue figures. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests.\n\n**Server:** the claimed totals in `rollup/Rollup.java` now use a new rule, `countsClaimed`, in `claim/ClaimFigures.java`. It counts the same claims as before but ignores holds. Due-total and overdue-total still use the old rule (`countsLive`), so held claims still leave those.\n\n**Front end:** `sumOf` in `features/claims/claims.ts` drives both `person-claimed` and `rollup-claimed-total`, and now uses the same hold-ignoring rule. Everything else that totals claims on screen keeps leaving held claims out.\n\n**Two other rules are unchanged:**\n- **Retirement:** once a person's retirement date is reached, their open claims still drop out of claimed, as before. The request only covered holds; the test passes this way.\n- **Deferral:** a deferred claim still leaves claimed. The test expects this (Ben's claimed goes to 0.00 after the defer).\n\nI also updated the comments in those files to match. The test output shows an older version of the `Rollup.java` comment because it printed before I fixed the wording; the file has the corrected one.",
